# Accord P0 — Binding Rules

You are the primary implementer for Magnus Accord. Read this before every task.

## The one rule that matters most

**R12 — Run every new check against the broken code and watch it fail, before you commit it.**

A check never observed failing is not evidence of anything. State it explicitly in your summary:
*"I ran this against the broken state and observed it fail."* If you can't, say why.

This is not theoretical. **Five vacuous gates were found in this repo in a single day** — every one
would have shipped as proof of safety:

1. `pnpm test` — the release gate; ran zero tests, exited 0
2. An `/app` redirect check — passed against a build with **no middleware at all**, because a
   server component emitted the identical redirect
3. `update:\s*\{[^}]*passwordHash` — `[^}]*` stopped at a nested `{ name }`, so it went green
   against the live password-overwrite bug it existed to catch
4. A test calling `createCampaignCheckoutSession` — a plausible name for a function that doesn't exist
5. A denial test whose payload omitted required fields, so it failed on input validation before
   ever reaching the guard under test

Assume you are about to write the sixth. Check.

## Known traps in this codebase

- **`validate-migrations.js` doesn't strip SQL comments.** A comment containing the words
  `DROP TABLE`, `DROP COLUMN`, or `RENAME COLUMN` fails the gate. Word migration comments around it.
- **Postgres refuses a new enum value in the same transaction that added it.** Adding an enum value
  and using it as a `DEFAULT` requires **two separate migrations**. Verified: a combined one fails
  with `unsafe use of new value`.
- **`subscriptionStatus` now defaults to `PENDING`.** Test fixtures that create an `Organization`
  without stating a status will be denied at entitlement gates. **R13: fixtures state their own
  preconditions** — never inherit a security-relevant value from a schema default.
- **`isFeatureEnabled` checks status before tier and fails closed** (`packages/subscription/src/policy.ts`).
  Any non-`ACTIVE` status is denied. Do not add a tier-only lookup — `getOrgTier` already exists
  with zero callers and is exactly that bypass.
- **Middleware must live at `apps/web/src/middleware.ts`**, beside `src/app/`. At the app root it
  compiles to nothing, silently. Assert against `.next/server/middleware-manifest.json`, not source.
- **`node --test <dir>` is unreliable here.** Use explicit globs plus `scripts/assert-test-count.js`
  with a `--min` floor, so a glob matching zero files fails instead of passing.
- **Never `prisma db push` against a deployed environment.** It writes objects without
  `_prisma_migrations` history. Staging hit `P3009` on `7430ad0` for this reason. Use
  `pnpm --filter @magnus/db prisma:deploy` from the app service that has the checkout.

## Hard constraints

- **Never handle credentials.** Not Stripe keys, not `DATABASE_URL`, not tokens. Don't read them,
  echo them, or write them to a file. If a task needs one, stop and ask the operator to place it.
- **No direct pushes to `main`.** Branch, PR, then merge only if `node scripts/merge-authority.js` exits 0 (CI green, base `main`, diff touches only `docs/**`). Anything else — including this policy file — is operator merge.
- **Merge is not deploy.** Never treat merge authorisation as deploy authorisation.
- **Additive-only migrations.** No DROP, no RENAME.
- **Money is integer minor units.** Never a float, never `Number()` on a `Decimal` column.
- **Absent data is `null` + provenance**, never `0`, never a random id, never a synthesized identity.
- **Every entitlement change writes an audit row in the same transaction.** If the audit write
  fails, the grant fails. There is no `--force`.
- **`orgId` scoping is a security boundary**, not a UI filter.
- **A public identifier is not authorisation.** EINs are published by the IRS.

## Working style for this repo

- Read the actual file before claiming what it does. Several findings in this project came from
  reading source that contradicted the documentation.
- Report what you observed, not what you expect. If you didn't run it, say you didn't run it.
- If a tool you were told to use isn't available, **stop and report** — do not substitute a more
  powerful one. (A read-only investigation once correctly halted rather than improvising into a
  shell. That was the right call.)
- Prefer one small PR that lands over a large one that stalls.
